course: dictionary
lesson: 4180
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it: this is the context. «The monkeys have golden fur» tells you about colour, because fur is not made of gold.
explain: «She found a tiny golden key under the table.» Could a key be made of gold? Yes, a key is a thing you can hold, so golden here means made of gold. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence best.
explain: Golden can also mean very special, as in «a golden chance». Nobody means the chance is metal! Try each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: Golden means made of gold, like a golden crown.
fact: Golden means having the bright yellow colour of gold, like golden hair, golden sand or golden toast.
fact: Golden means very special, happy or excellent, as in «a golden chance».
fact: «The golden rule» means treat others as you want to be treated.
fact: A golden retriever is a friendly dog with golden fur.
exercise: «The monkeys in the snowy mountains have golden fur.» What does golden mean here? | Cold and white | Made of gold, like a coin | Very special and excellent | *Having the bright yellow colour of gold
exercise: «She found a tiny golden key under the table.» What does golden mean here? | Shiny and soft | Having the bright yellow colour of gold | Very special and excellent | *Made of gold
exercise: «Ella got a golden chance to sing in the school show.» What does golden mean here? | *Very special and excellent | Shiny and cold | Made of gold | Having a yellow colour
test: «The sunset turned the sky a golden orange.» Which meaning fits best? | *Having the bright yellow colour of gold | Very special and excellent | Made of gold metal | Cold and dark
test: Ben says the golden rule is a rule about gold coins. What is the golden rule? | Always wear yellow clothes | *Treat others as you want to be treated | Keep your gold safe at home | Only buy gold things
exam: In «a golden chance», what does golden mean? | Hard and shiny | Made of gold | Having the colour of gold | *Very special and excellent
